  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Ku Mu mountain reads as a giant dead wooden tree extending into the clouds. The wood’s name is old earth. This pillar has more than a million years of history, from Reckless Savage Demon Venerable’s era through Red Lotus Demon Venerable, Genesis Lotus Immortal Venerable, Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable, Giant Sun Immortal Venerable, Spectral Soul Demon Venerable, and Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable, and it remains alive after Paradise Earth Immortal Venerable dies.",
      "chapters": [
        738
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_ku_mu_mountain",
        "char_reckless_savage_demon_venerable",
        "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable",
        "char_genesis_lotus_immortal_venerable",
        "char_thieving_heaven_demon_venerable",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "char_spectral_soul_demon_venerable",
        "char_paradise_earth_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In its lush years, greenery covered the sky, it produced countless fresh fruits, and strong branches could hold unique tree farms. The strongest Gu Immortals or most powerful forces in Northern Plains usually owned it then. Later the green leaves wilt, the trunk decays, and barren branches shade only a small area. The main trunk is mostly dead; only a small portion still has a little life left. Forces once fought and died over it; in its late years it sits lonely with few visitors.",
      "chapters": [
        738
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "reg_northern_plains"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Old Earth City stands on its branches. Gu Ye holds a Zombie Alliance mission to guard old earth wood, and wilted essence still comes from the place.",
      "chapters": [
        738
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_old_earth_city",
        "char_gu_ye",
        "fac_zombie_alliance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Using Looking Back Immortal Gu in the area of the old earth wood would allow one to see the former glorious scenery.",
      "chapters": [
        746
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "looking-back-site",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_looking_back_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ku Mu Mountain is named as the most famous example of old earth wood: not an ordinary mountain, but an old earth wood tree. Primordial Origin Immortal Venerable’s lifespan of twenty five thousand years, the longest among venerables in that comparison, and Red Lotus Demon Venerable’s three thousand years, are barely a fraction of that tree’s lifespan.",
      "chapters": [
        994
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "lifespan-comparison",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_primordial_origin_immortal_venerable"
      ]
    }
  ],
